# ==============================================================================
# RAZORAGENT MESH — ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION TEMPLATE
# ==============================================================================
# Every variable below is read by code. Copy this file to .env and edit.
# docker-compose.yml sets each service's port and Redis URL directly, so a Docker
# run needs far less of this than a bare-metal one.

# Razorpay Test Mode Credentials.
# Read by packages/mandateEngine/config.py. These two decide the settlement transport:
# buildRouteClient selects the LIVE Razorpay Route API as soon as RAZORPAY_KEY_ID is not one of
# the placeholders ("", rzp_test_mock, rzp_test_MockApiKey12345) and the secret is non-empty.
# The value below is a placeholder, so it keeps settlement on the deterministic mock ledger.
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=rzp_test_MockApiKey12345
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=MockApiSecretKey67890

# Infrastructure Endpoints
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0

# Read by packages/merchantApi (src/merchantApp.py) to build the Qdrant client its
# auto-vectorizer indexes published SKUs with, and by scripts/seedCatalog.py.
QDRANT_HOST=localhost
QDRANT_PORT=6333

# Ed25519 Cryptographic Keys (Hex Seeds)
# Deliberately EMPTY. An empty value makes packages/mcpServer fall back to the development key
# committed in src/constants/protocolConstants.ts, and the server says so at startup. Shipping a
# real-looking value here instead would silence that warning while still using a key that anyone
# with this repository has -- the worst of both. Set a generated key for anything shared:
#   python scripts/generateTestKeys.py
MERCHANT_PRIVATE_KEY_HEX=

# Layer 1 MCP Quote HMAC Signing Key.
# Same rule as above: empty selects the committed demo key and warns. Every peer that verifies
# quote signatures must use the SAME value -- if this is set for one service and not another,
# quotes sign with one key and verify with another, and every quote silently fails verification.
HMAC_SECRET_KEY=

# Layer 5 Telemetry SSE Endpoint
NEXT_PUBLIC_TELEMETRY_SSE_URL=http://localhost:8000/api/v1/telemetry/stream

# Service URLs. The telemetry dashboard's protocol driver
# (src/server/protocolDriver/driverConfig.ts) resolves each service from these, falling back to
# localhost. The MCP server also reads MANDATE_ENGINE_URL to publish tool activity, so an
# external agent's calls appear on the dashboard instead of only its final settlement -- that one
# is optional, and a missing bus never fails a tool call.
MANDATE_ENGINE_URL=http://localhost:8000
MCP_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:4001
MERCHANT_API_URL=http://localhost:4002
X402_GATEWAY_URL=http://localhost:4003

# HTTP port for packages/mcpServer (src/http/httpAdapter.ts). The three FastAPI services take
# their port from their Dockerfile's uvicorn command, not from the environment.
PORT=4001

# Which git branch the dashboard's docs pages link "view source" at.
# Read by packages/telemetryDashboard/src/constants/docsSourceConfig.ts.
# DOCS_SOURCE_BRANCH=main

# MCP transport selection for packages/mcpServer: stdio | http | both (default both).
# Set to "stdio" when launching the server from an MCP client while the Docker mesh is
# already serving port 4001, so the second copy does not try to bind it.
# MCP_TRANSPORT=both

# Test seam for packages/mandateEngine. When true, /api/v1/settlement/execute accepts any
# serverTime instead of requiring it to sit near the real clock. NEVER enable this outside a test
# run: serverTime overrides mandate expiry, inventory-lock expiry, the NTP drift window,
# cumulative-spend expiry and the date on the GSTR-1 invoice, so a caller who can set it freely
# can settle an expired mandate and back-date a statutory invoice.
# ALLOW_CLIENT_SERVER_TIME=false

# Layer 2 Price-Drop Webhook SSRF Guard
# Agent-supplied callbackUrl values must be HTTPS with a public host. Private,
# loopback, link-local and reserved addresses (including the 169.254.169.254
# cloud metadata endpoint) are always rejected.
# Set to "true" ONLY for local demos, to additionally permit http://localhost
# callbacks. Leave unset/false in every deployed environment.
# ALLOW_LOCALHOST_CALLBACK=false

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Removed, and why: GATEWAY_SECRET, BUYER_AGENT_PRIVATE_KEY_HEX,
# USER_CFO_PRIVATE_KEY_HEX and MERCHANT_API_PORT were listed here but read by nothing.
# GATEWAY_SECRET's comment claimed it "defaults to a development value in
# packages/x402Gateway/src/config.py" -- X402GatewaySettings defines only redisUrl, so it
# described a mechanism that did not exist. Setting any of the four had no effect.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
